# regression.list - the named regression set (incidents-as-eval, card
# t_8abdbb15). Every recipe here once burned a lane and must never
# fail again. Format: one recipe per line, recipe FILE name first,
# then the red it pins (text only; the parser strips '#' comments).
#
# run.sh --regression executes exactly this set (gate-time minimum,
# lane SHA); the full suite - the nightly and every train pass - runs
# it as part of everything. A name here that no longer matches a
# recipe file is an ERROR, not a silent skip: a regression entry that
# rots quietly is the same as deleting the proof.
#
# The set also carries pin tests that are NOT journey recipes (a
# journey cannot see compile-time shape) - they run in go test ./...
# and in the train gate list, documented here so the set is complete:
#   - TestToggleConcurrentSharedFoldLock (cmd/omega/modules_test.go):
#     the shared-fold toggle race - lost updates under concurrent
#     toggles through the shared mutex (v0.14.0 release-gate must-fix).
#   - cmd/omega/purity_wires_test.go: the nm-purity wire-shape pins -
#     the verdict answer exchange stays in harness/verdict (no inline
#     ParseCardAnswer in cmd/, loop.go keeps the named-return wire) and
#     the wizard provider hook keeps its named return (bea6abc rotations).
#   - scripts/fence-test.sh: the worker fence eval - a worker session's
#     push/landing must refuse or be mechanically blocked; the eval
#     fails if the operation succeeds. Runs in the train gate list.
#   - scripts/journeys/console_scope_test.sh: the console-record scope pin
#     (t_6654bc60) - agent-browser's console buffer belongs to the DAEMON
#     SESSION (it survives navigation, reload and a reconnect to a
#     different chrome), so one transient [NUXT_E5002] red every later
#     assert_no_console_errors on that host while the manifest answered
#     200. run.sh now clears the record before each recipe forks; the test
#     drives the real run.sh with a stub browser and proves the old line
#     cannot red the next recipe, the unscoped shape still does, and a real
#     error from the recipe's own run still reds.
60-settings-themes t_31aa2542 - the Settings chip/knob poll contract: the cold-runner wait_js race (theme picker "got [0] want [1]") - poll, never a zero-wait query
61-session-title-fallback  t_8abdbb15 - session titles never lean on a model: the label renders with zero title runs; the unlabeled tab keeps the stable generic fallback (the nightly's no-provider reds, f82f4ee)
75-divider-resize  t_38c0e960 - dock-stuck divider shapes: the v0.9.0 drag rework crossed the cumulative/per-event delta contract - the divider looked dead (~10px per full drag)
50-sessions-reload  679c2458 - the search seat's narrowing: the capsule's literal GET /sessions/search died into the base /sessions/{id} wildcard behind the catch-all (id="search" answered "session not found"), the sidebar search never narrowed - the moduleLiterals rescue lane (2026-11-05 nightly)
98-kanban-drag-reorder  t_82e5d149 - the board switcher chip behind a ONCE-per-mount GET /boards fetch (Board.vue): a fetch missing under suite load (nightly run 42260775149, lane hiccup) left no chip for the whole page life and burned the recipe's two mounts - the mounted fetch now retries (3 attempts, ~300ms backoff); the recipe's poll+reload fallback stays the last resort. Dropped in the d73402e0 re-land; restored - the 4 CI reds (t_54dd7215) keep it named. t_96844dcb: the CI reds' real mechanism traced - a persisted browser pane (recipe 96's singleton in the main pane foreground) shadowed the /board route (Board.vue never mounted, the reload could not heal it); the foreground reclaim fix (fix(webui) 431690c9) keeps the recipe in the set as the pin.
111-socket-push.journey  t_71f28526 - the reconnect's catch-up refetch never ran (nightly run 43000140712, 2026-11-11, plus the reopened dev-lane red the same day): the quiet-wire cut fires at 15-16s of silence, but a half-open socket's close EVENT is deferred for the whole outage (measured under `ab set offline`, agent-browser 0.26.0 and 0.42.0) or never arrives, and the client scheduled its reconnect only from that event - dark page, no ladder, no /health+/sessions refetch, the row seeded while offline never showed. The cut now hands recovery to the ladder itself and the stale close is ignored (pinned in webui/test/socket.test.ts); this recipe is the browser-level half - no pollers, drop -> reconnect -> refetched pane.
93-provider-instances  t_2454597e - the api_key door (354ef12f) vs a stale recipe: the journey's save flow planted a plain-text instance key over the API, exactly the shape the door now refuses (nightly run 42426834227, Nov 8). The recipe now adds its instance keyless and PINS the refusal - plain-key PUTs (new row, stored row), a clear of a keyed lane row when the lane carries one, and the door error surfaced in the pane. A future door-removal turns this journey red instead of silently reopening the API.
114-tools-one-row  t_0c8d88f2 - the tools tab's duplicate sections (Endo, 2026-11-07: "why are there 2 `files` sections?"). t_7871a56a fixed the row model and pinned it in the node suite; this is the browser-level half - exactly ONE "files" row carrying read/write/edit/glob/grep as absorbed detail, no domain rendered twice, no detail line under a foreign row, and the fold-aware round-trip (disable the domain -> the row STAYS dimmed and toggleable, bare /tools drops it, /tools?disabled=1 keeps all six stamped; re-enable clears the fold on the wire and in the lane home's config.yaml).
113-settings-nav.journey  t_c4b42357 - a flat (or one-child) category emits its data-section id TWICE (the section and its single unheaded block), and the spy/clamp map kept the LAST match: jumping to `common`, `dock` or `store` parked the block's top at y=0 under the section's own opaque sticky heading, and the clamp - measuring the block instead of the section - snapped the pane back when the user scrolled up to reveal the hidden row. The map is now built SECTIONS FIRST (webui/app/components/settings/settingsNav.ts buildSpyTargets, pinned in webui/test/settingsnav.test.ts) and the recipe measures BOTH rects after each jump: the first knob row starts below the pinned heading's bottom. Ran only in the nightly before this, which is why the bug reached a release.
84-terminal-divider-tracks  t_8098aa06 - the fixed lanes' absorb never ran: a drag wrote only the FIXED pane's px and flexbox reflow spread the delta over every flexible child, so the terminal's right divider on its INWARD leg moved the 220px terminal just 20px for a 60px drag (Endo, 2026-11-13) - and the chat, which the gesture never touched, moved too. absorbNeighbor now re-splits the two-child pair so the adjacent pane lands on pairPx - fixedPx and every other flex sibling holds its frozen px (pinned in webui/test/dividerabsorb.test.ts); this recipe is the browser-level half - all four legs 1:1, and "right divider inward: got [200] want [160] (tol 2)" before the fix.
